/-
# SINGLE-LETTER CONTEXT-FREE LANGUAGE MEMBERSHIP is NP-complete

Source:
D. S. Johnson, "The NP-completeness column: an ongoing guide", J. Algorithms 4 (1983), 87-100,
doi:10.1016/0196-6774(83)90038-X, problem [2] SINGLE-LETTER CONTEXT-FREE LANGUAGE MEMBERSHIP
(reference: Huynh at FOCS-82; transformation from SUBSET SUM);
D. T. Huynh, "Deciding the inequivalence of context-free grammars with 1-letter terminal
alphabet is Σ₂ᵖ-complete", Proc. 23rd Annual Symposium on Foundations of Computer Science
(1982), 21-31, doi:10.1109/SFCS.1982.65, and Theoretical Computer Science 33 (1984), 305-326,
doi:10.1016/0304-3975(84)90092-6.
-/
module

public import Batteries.Util.ProofWanted
public import CSLibExt.Computability.CookLevin
public import MathlibExt.Computability.BinaryNatEncoding
public import MathlibExt.Computability.Complexity
public import WantedExt.Complexity.NPComplete.QuasiRealTimeLanguageMembershipWanted

@[expose] public section

namespace MetaMathlibExt.Complexity.NPComplete.SingleLetterCFLMembership

open MetaMathlibExt.Complexity.NPComplete.QuasiRealTimeLanguageMembership
  (GrammarData toEncodedCFG GrammarWellFormed)

/-!
# SINGLE-LETTER CONTEXT-FREE LANGUAGE MEMBERSHIP is NP-complete

INSTANCE: a context-free grammar `G = (N, Σ, Π, S)`, where the set `Σ` of terminal symbols has
one element `w`, and a positive integer `K`. QUESTION: is the string `x = wᴷ` in the language
generated by `G`?

The terminal alphabet is `Σ = {0}`, so `w` is the terminal `0` and `wᴷ` is
`List.replicate K 0`. The nonterminals of a grammar with `n` nonterminals are `0, ..., n - 1`. A
production is a pair of a left-hand side and a list of right-hand side symbols, in which
`(false, B)` is nonterminal `B` and `(true, a)` is terminal `a`; the set of productions is a list
(a repeated production does not change the grammar), and right-hand sides may be empty. The
grammar is read as a `Cslib.Language.EncodedCFG`, whose language is that of a Mathlib
`ContextFreeGrammar` with nonterminals `ℕ`. This grammar encoding (`GrammarData`,
`toEncodedCFG`, `GrammarWellFormed`) is the one of
`WantedExt.Complexity.NPComplete.QuasiRealTimeLanguageMembershipWanted`, reused here.

`K` is encoded in binary, so the string `wᴷ` itself is not part of the input; the problem is
solvable in pseudo-polynomial time by standard parsing and is NP-complete in the ordinary (weak)
sense.

Encoding: the instance is decoded from a bitstring with the repository's
canonical `MetaMathlibExt.BitstringEncoding`. Undecodable bitstrings, and
bitstrings decoding to malformed instances, are no-instances.

NP-completeness is stated in the same form as the proved results in
`CSLibExt.Computability.Complexity.Karp`: membership in
`MetaMathlibExt.ComplexityTheory.NP`, plus a polynomial-time many-one
reduction from every language in `NP`
(`Cslib.CookLevin.PolyManyOneRed`).
-/

/-- An instance: the grammar `G` over the one-letter alphabet `{0}` and the exponent `K`. -/
abbrev SingleLetterCFLMembershipInstance := GrammarData × ℕ

/-- Well-formedness of an instance: the grammar is well-formed over the one-letter terminal
alphabet `{0}`, and `K` is positive. -/
def WellFormed (i : SingleLetterCFLMembershipInstance) : Prop :=
  GrammarWellFormed 1 i.1 ∧ 0 < i.2

/-- The string `wᴷ` (`K` copies of the terminal `0`) is generated by `G`. -/
def SingleLetterCFLMembershipFeasible (i : SingleLetterCFLMembershipInstance) : Prop :=
  List.replicate i.2 0 ∈ (toEncodedCFG i.1).language

open Classical in
/-- SINGLE-LETTER CONTEXT-FREE LANGUAGE MEMBERSHIP as a decision problem over bitstrings. -/
noncomputable def singleLetterCFLMembershipDec :
    MetaMathlibExt.ComplexityTheory.DecisionProblem := fun x =>
  match MetaMathlibExt.BitstringEncoding.bitDecode
      (α := SingleLetterCFLMembershipInstance) x with
  | some i => decide (WellFormed i ∧ SingleLetterCFLMembershipFeasible i)
  | none => false

/-- **SINGLE-LETTER CONTEXT-FREE LANGUAGE MEMBERSHIP is NP-complete.** Source: Johnson,
NP-completeness column (1983), problem [2]; Huynh (1982, 1984). -/
public theorem_wanted singleLetterCFLMembership_npComplete :
    singleLetterCFLMembershipDec ∈ MetaMathlibExt.ComplexityTheory.NP ∧
      ∀ L : MetaMathlibExt.ComplexityTheory.DecisionProblem,
        L ∈ MetaMathlibExt.ComplexityTheory.NP →
          Cslib.CookLevin.PolyManyOneRed L singleLetterCFLMembershipDec

end MetaMathlibExt.Complexity.NPComplete.SingleLetterCFLMembership
